In Plain Sight — licensing at a glance
======================================

This repository is deliberately fork-friendly. Three licenses apply, by
component, so that both the code and the writing are clearly reusable:

  Code                  MIT              -> LICENSE
                        Astro components, TypeScript, JavaScript, CSS,
                        build scripts, configuration.

  Content and data      CC BY 4.0        -> LICENSE-CONTENT
                        Markdown prose, page and card copy, compiled
                        datasets under src/data/ and language-access/,
                        research notes.

  Bundled webfonts      SIL Open Font License 1.1 (NOT MIT, NOT CC BY)
                        Everything under public/fonts/ is redistributed
                        under its own upstream license and is not covered
                        by this project's grants:
                          Newsreader     (c) The Newsreader Project Authors
                          Public Sans    (c) The Public Sans Project Authors
                          IBM Plex Mono  (c) IBM Corp.
                        Full OFL text: https://openfontlicense.org

Not covered by any grant here
-----------------------------
  * The typeface "Redaction" (MCKL) is NOT bundled and NOT licensed for this
    project. The site ships on Newsreader. If a fork wants Redaction, it must
    license it independently from MCKL.
  * Source material quoted from District of Columbia government publications
    (regulations, meeting minutes, transcripts, notices) is government work
    reproduced for public-interest purposes; it carries whatever status it had
    at the source and is not relicensed by this repository.
  * The name "In Plain Sight" and the three-stars-and-two-bars mark are used
    as project identity. Forks are asked to follow the naming convention in
    FORKING.md rather than to present themselves as the DC instance.

